helm-website-ui/
helm-intelligence/
next-shadcn-dashboard-starter/
archive/
.full-review/
.full-review-archive-*/
.full-stack-feature-archived-*/

# Local-only artifacts
docs/superpowers/
*.pptx

# Build + test output.
#
# These are already in .gitignore, which would normally be enough — but the
# MOMENT this file exists, Vercel uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore rather than in
# addition to it. So everything .gitignore was quietly keeping out of the
# upload came back the first time anyone ran `vercel --prod` from a working
# directory that had been built or tested in.
#
# That is not theoretical: a deploy on 2026-08-03 was rejected outright —
#   "`files` should NOT have more than 15000 items, received 48139"
# — because .next alone was 13 GB of Turbopack cache at the time.
.next/
node_modules/
test-results/
playwright-report/
coverage/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local-only tooling state — same .gitignore-is-ignored trap as the block
# above, and the reason the 2026-08-09 deploy was rejected at 19,795 files:
#
#   .deepsec    26,425 files — per-repo security-scanner working directory
#   .worktrees   7,004 files — git worktrees, i.e. a FULL SOURCE COPY of every
#                              in-flight branch, uploaded alongside the branch
#                              actually being deployed
#
# Both are in .gitignore and neither has ever been part of a build. Listing
# them here is what makes .gitignore's intent apply to the upload too.
.deepsec/
.worktrees/
# .claude/worktrees/ is the SAME hazard as .worktrees/ above, at a new address:
# Claude Code's own worktree tooling creates them here now rather than in the
# repo-root .worktrees/ this file already covered. Measured 2026-08-19: 5.0 GB
# and ~44,000 .ts/.tsx across 12 trees, against src/'s 3,888 — an order of
# magnitude more source than the app itself.
#
# This is not hypothetical tidiness. `scripts/deploy-prod.sh` uploads the local
# tree, and production deploys began failing outright with
# "Request body too large. Limit: 10mb" until this line existed.
.claude/worktrees/

# Untracked local artifact directories. Same .gitignore-is-ignored trap as the
# blocks above, and measured 2026-08-20 during a production promote that STALLED
# at "Uploading (0.0B/1.6GB)" and never moved:
#
#   audit/   1,070 MB — audit + research output, 0 files tracked by git
#   tools/      71 MB — local tooling checkouts
#
# Neither has ever been part of a build. `audit/` alone was two thirds of the
# upload. The deploy that stalled on it produced a Canceled PREVIEW and never
# moved the production alias — i.e. it looked like a deploy and shipped nothing,
# which is the exact failure this repo keeps re-learning.
audit/
tools/

# More untracked local artifact directories — the SAME trap as audit/ and
# tools/ above, at new addresses. Every one of these is in .gitignore and
# untracked, which is exactly why they upload: the moment this file exists
# Vercel consults it INSTEAD of .gitignore, so "git ignores it" stops meaning
# "Vercel ignores it". Measured 2026-08-31, all five together: 166 files, 21 MB.
#
#   .playwright-mcp   browser session logs from a debugging run in August
#   .agents           local agent skill definitions
#   routes            generated route dumps and a wiki export
#   .ruff_cache       linter cache
#   .momentic-mcp     tooling state
#
# None has ever been a build input.
.playwright-mcp/
.agents/
routes/
.ruff_cache/
.momentic-mcp/
# Tracked, unlike the five above, but still pure test artifacts (jpegs from
# MCP CLI runs) that no build step reads.
.momentic/

# Documentation. 1,698 tracked files and 145 MB — 54% of the entire upload,
# and more than half of that is binary: marketing mockup references, visual-audit
# screenshots, PDFs.
#
# Nothing in the build reads it. Verified 2026-08-31: no reference in
# next.config.mjs, tailwind.config.ts, tsconfig.json or package.json; no import
# from src/; no /docs route; no runtime readFile against it. Next.js serves
# static assets from public/, which is separate and stays.
#
# This excludes docs from the UPLOAD only. They remain tracked in git, which is
# where they are actually read.
docs/

# Secrets. This is the .gitignore-is-ignored trap at its worst address.
#
# .gitignore keeps the .env family out of git, and that is the ONLY thing that
# was keeping it out of the upload too — so the moment this file appeared,
# Vercel stopped consulting .gitignore and every `vercel deploy` began shipping
# them off this machine. Measured 2026-08-31 by simulating the upload set
# against this file: .env, .env.local, .env.development.local and
# .env.production.local were all in it. .env.local is the one that carries
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, HELM_PROD_POSTGRES_PASSWORD and
# HELM_PROD_DB_URL_DIRECT — the credentials .claude/rules/shipping.md calls the
# path that "nothing intercepts".
#
# Runtime env comes from Vercel's own project settings, never from an uploaded
# file, so excluding these changes nothing about how the app runs.
.env
.env.*
# .env.example is documentation and carries no live values — keep it.
!.env.example

# The .env family was not the only secret the same trap was shipping. Measured
# 2026-09-01, each of these is gitignored, PRESENT on disk in the canonical
# checkout, and was in the upload set until this block:
#
#   .cursor/mcp.json          an sbp_ Supabase access token (.gitleaks.toml
#                             added a rule for that shape on 2026-08-19 and
#                             names this exact file)
#   context7.json             a Context7 api_key (.gitignore names it)
#   playwright/.auth/         Playwright storage state — Supabase session
#                             cookies for real accounts
#   momentic/auth/            Momentic test-account auth + .momentic.env
#   android/keystore.properties  the upload keystore password
#   *.keystore / *.jks / *.pem   signing keys and certificates, wherever they sit
#   .claude/settings.local.json  the per-machine allowlist that once reached
#                             this public repo (.gitignore's own note)
#   .claude/session-state/    per-session ledgers and the release marker
#   .vercel/                  the project link (orgId/projectId)
#   supabase/.temp/           linked project ref + CLI scratch
#
# config/repo/manifest.yml → vercel.must_ignore is the maintained list, and
# `npm run check:vercelignore` (repo:doctor, and CI's control-plane job) fails
# when any entry there is not matched here. Add to BOTH when a new secret-
# bearing path is gitignored — the manifest is what makes this file checkable.
.cursor/
context7.json
playwright/.auth/
momentic/auth/
android/keystore.properties
*.keystore
*.jks
*.pem
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.local.json.*
.claude/session-state/
.vercel/
supabase/.temp/

# Local-only artifact directories found present on 2026-09-01 by the same
# sweep. None is a build input; the largest (.dev-assets, 13 MB) is the
# screenshot/deck scratch .gitignore moved out of the repo root on 2026-08-03.
# deno.lock is regenerated by `npm run typecheck:functions` and is a manifest
# for edge functions the Vercel build never compiles.
.dev-assets/
.dev-screenshots/
.codex/
.design-sync/
.ultracode/
.vscode/
.idea/
deno.lock

# Native shell — built by Capacitor/Xcode, never by the Vercel build.
android/
ios/
